w, 640px" /><p>
	<div class="smittenkitchen-print-hide">
			</div>

	It is an error that needs correcting that in the near-20 years of plugging recipes into this url, only a few truly star <a href="https://smittenkitchen.com/recipes/vegetable/cucumber/">cucumbers</a> &#8212; and highly unrepresentative too, given that we are probably eating some format of cucumbers at half the nights of the week with dinner, and snacking on them throughout all of the other days. Crunchy, cold, hydrating, inexpensive, and taking well to any region of ingredients you wish to apply, I don&#8217;t need to sell you on their appeal, especially as we slog through our <em>n</em>th heat wave of the summer. I suspect that the lack of cucumber representation in the archives has more to do with the fact that little about cucumber salads brings out my inner obsessive recipe finetuner; usually I&#8217;m just throwing it together.</p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="https://i0.wp.com/live.staticflickr.com/65535/55460059645_4f2217e637_z.jpg?resize=640%2C427&#038;quality=89&#038;ssl=1" alt="cucumber salad with sesame-1" width="640" height="427" /></p>
